TITLE:: RLMetre
summary:: Metre as a relation on a cycle of pulses, and rhythmic canons
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLRelation, Classes/RLRelationContext, Classes/RLAutomorphism, Classes/RLTimeSpans, Classes/RCSieve, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
On a cycle of n pulses, the metre M(d) relates two pulses a multiple of d apart (Popoff and Yust). Metres are link::Classes/RLRelation::s and their algebra is arithmetic: composing two gives their greatest common divisor, intersecting them their least common multiple, and one is included in another when its number is a multiple of the other's. Shifting the pulses, or multiplying them by a number prime to n, changes no metre: they are automorphisms of the context (link::Classes/RLAutomorphism::).

A rhythmic strong::canon:: is a rhythm A and a set of entries B that tile the cycle: every pulse sounded once.

code::
~m = RLMetre(12);
(~m.relation(4) <> ~m.relation(6)) == ~m.relation(2);      // true: the gcd
(~m.relation(4) & ~m.relation(6)) == ~m.relation(12);      // true: the lcm
~m.relation(4) <= ~m.relation(2);                          // true: 4 is a multiple of 2

~ctx = ~m.context([4, 6]);                                 // M4 and M6 by name
~ctx.category.size;                                        // 4: the identity, M4, M6, M2
RLAutomorphism(~ctx, { |x| (x * 5) % 12 }).isValid;        // true

~m.tiles([0, 1, 2], [0, 3, 6, 9]);                         // true
~m.complements([0, 1, 5]);                                 // [[0, 3, 6, 9]]
~m.complements([0, 1, 3]);                                 // []: no canon on this rhythm
RLMetre(16).complements([0, 1, 4, 5]);                     // [[0, 2, 8, 10], [0, 6, 8, 14]]
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: n
The number of pulses in the cycle.

METHOD:: perfect
Perfect tilings: a rhythm played by a number of voices, each at a stretch of its own, tiling the line of code::rhythm.size * voices:: pulses. code::[stretches, entries]:: pairs. For three pulses in a row there is none before five voices.
code::
RLMetre.perfect([0, 1, 2], 5);      // 15 pulses, stretches 1, 2, 4, 5, 7, entering at 10, 2, 1, 3, 0 or at 2, 8, 5, 1, 0
::

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: n
METHOD:: points
The pulses, code::[0, 1 ... n - 1]::.

METHOD:: relation
The metre M(d): two pulses a multiple of d apart (round the cycle, a multiple of the gcd of d and n).

METHOD:: context
The pulses with several metres as relations named code::\M2::, code::\M3::...: an link::Classes/RLRelationContext::.

METHOD:: tiles
Whether a rhythm (a list of pulses), entering at each of the entries, sounds every pulse of the cycle once.

METHOD:: complements
Every set of entries, the pulse 0 among them, with which a rhythm tiles the cycle.

METHOD:: augmented
A canon by augmentation on the line of the n pulses (not round the cycle): one voice per stretch plays the rhythm d times as slow from its entry, and every pulse is sounded once. Every list of entries, in the order of the stretches. With link::Classes/RLTimeSpans#-canon::, the voice of stretch d entering at u is the rhythm under the left element code::[u, d]::.
code::
RLMetre(12).augmented([0, 1, 2], [1, 1, 2, 2]);     // [[0, 3, 6, 7], [0, 9, 3, 4], [6, 9, 0, 1]]
::
